Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adb: tls: include <string.h> for strerror()

tls_connection.cpp calls strerror() without including <string.h>; it builds
on Android because bionic/libc++ headers pull it in transitively, but not
with GCC and libstdc++:

  tls/tls_connection.cpp:334:46: error: 'strerror' was not declared in this scope

Upstream-Status: Pending

AI-Generated: Claude Opus 5.5 (Claude Code)
Signed-off-by: Alex Kiernan <alex.kiernan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/packages/modules/adb/tls/tls_connection.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/tls/tls_connection.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include "adb/tls/tls_connection.h"
 
 #include <limits.h>
+#include <string.h>
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <vector>
